From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:02:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: fall back to pp done when there is no CTL_START
 interrupt

Not every DPU generates a CTL_START interrupt: on MSM8998 the downstream
driver defines only the two PP CWB overflow bits in INTR2, and on a
Pixel 2 XL the 9..13 bits never assert while frames demonstrably complete
(PP_LINE_COUNT reaches vdisplay and the DSI raises CMD_MDP_DONE). The irq
registration paths already skip a zero irq index, but
wait_for_commit_done() still waited on the missing interrupt whenever the
CTL_START readback had already self-cleared, so every commit timed out.
Wait for pp done instead when the catalog declares no start interrupt.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
index 0ec6d67c7c70..bdd80bf68615 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
@@ -681,7 +681,9 @@ static int dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_wait_for_commit_done(
 	if (!dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_is_master(phys_enc))
 		return 0;
 
-	if (phys_enc->hw_ctl->ops.is_started(phys_enc->hw_ctl))
+	/* Hardware without a CTL_START interrupt can only wait on pp done */
+	if (!phys_enc->irq[INTR_IDX_CTL_START] ||
+	    phys_enc->hw_ctl->ops.is_started(phys_enc->hw_ctl))
 		return dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_wait_for_tx_complete(phys_enc);
 
 	return _dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_wait_for_ctl_start(phys_enc);
